QUESTION_PROMPT_BEGIN bytes=804
An intelligent civilization in the Large Magellanic Cloud has engineered an extraordinary spacecraft capable of traveling at a substantial fraction of the speed of light. The average lifetime of these aliens is roughly 150 solar years. Now, having Earth as their destination in mind, they are determined to travel with this spacecraft at a constant speed of 0.99999987*c, where c is the speed of light. Approximately, how long will it take for their 22 years old astronaut (from the point of view of the astronaut) to reach the Earth using this incredibly fast spacecraft?

Choices:
A. 72 years
B. 81 years
C. The astronaut will die before reaching to the Earth.
D. 77 years

Solve the question. At the end, write exactly one final line in this format and do not write anything after it:
Answer: <letter>
QUESTION_PROMPT_END
MODEL_OUTPUT_BEGIN bytes=1393
We need to compute the proper time experienced by the astronaut traveling at v = 0.99999987c. The distance from the Large Magellanic Cloud to Earth is about 160,000 light-years. However, the problem doesn't give the distance explicitly—it gives the aliens' average lifetime (150 solar years) and the astronaut's age (22 years). The question is about whether the astronaut will survive the trip.

The key is relativistic time dilation. For the astronaut, the time experienced (proper time) is the Earth-frame travel time divided by the Lorentz factor γ.

γ = 1 / sqrt(1 - v²/c²)  
v/c = 0.99999987  
1 - (v/c)² = 1 - (0.99999987)²  
(0.99999987)² = 0.9999997400001369 (approx)  
1 - that = 0.0000002599998631  
sqrt = about 0.0005099  
γ ≈ 1 / 0.0005099 ≈ 1961

So time is dilated by factor ~1961.

If the distance is ~160,000 light-years, Earth-frame travel time = distance / v ≈ 160,000 / 0.99999987 ≈ 160,000 years (slightly more).  
Proper time for astronaut = 160,000 / 1961 ≈ 81.6 years.

The astronaut is 22 years old, so after 81.6 years proper time, they will be about 103.6 years old. The average alien lifetime is 150 years, so they will survive.

Thus the trip takes about 81 years from the astronaut's perspective.

The choices:  
A. 72 years  
B. 81 years  
C. The astronaut will die before reaching Earth.  
D. 77 years

The closest is B. 81 years.

Answer: B
MODEL_OUTPUT_END

