QUESTION_PROMPT_BEGIN bytes=618
For a magnetic field \vec{B}, parallel to Oz, with small values of m (orbital magnetic quantum number) and B=1T, compare the order of magnitude of the paramagnetic coupling term with transition energy \Delta E of Hydrogen atom with wavelength \lambda=0.4861\mu m.

PS: for the maths use an online LaTeX editor.

Choices:
A. \left\langle H\right\rangle =\Delta E
B. \left\langle H\right\rangle \ll\Delta E
C. \left\langle H\right\rangle \gg\Delta E
D. \left\langle H\right\rangle >\Delta E

Solve the question. At the end, write exactly one final line in this format and do not write anything after it:
Answer: <letter>
QUESTION_PROMPT_END
MODEL_OUTPUT_BEGIN bytes=1335
We are asked to compare the paramagnetic coupling term \(\langle H \rangle\) with the transition energy \(\Delta E\) for a hydrogen atom transition with wavelength \(\lambda = 0.4861 \, \mu\text{m}\).  

First, compute \(\Delta E\):  
\[
\Delta E = \frac{hc}{\lambda}
\]  
Using \(h = 6.626 \times 10^{-34} \, \text{J·s}\), \(c = 3 \times 10^8 \, \text{m/s}\), \(\lambda = 0.4861 \times 10^{-6} \, \text{m}\):  
\[
\Delta E \approx \frac{(6.626 \times 10^{-34})(3 \times 10^8)}{0.4861 \times 10^{-6}} \approx 4.09 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{J}
\]  
In eV: \(1 \, \text{eV} = 1.602 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{J}\), so  
\[
\Delta E \approx \frac{4.09 \times 10^{-19}}{1.602 \times 10^{-19}} \approx 2.55 \, \text{eV}
\]  

Now the paramagnetic coupling term for a magnetic field \(B = 1 \, \text{T}\) along Oz:  
\[
H_{\text{paramagnetic}} = -\vec{\mu} \cdot \vec{B} = -\mu_B \, m_l \, B
\]  
where \(\mu_B = 9.274 \times 10^{-24} \, \text{J/T}\) and \(m_l\) is small (say \(|m_l| \le 1\)).  
Order of magnitude:  
\[
|\langle H \rangle| \approx \mu_B B \approx 9.274 \times 10^{-24} \, \text{J}
\]  
In eV:  
\[
\frac{9.274 \times 10^{-24}}{1.602 \times 10^{-19}} \approx 5.79 \times 10^{-5} \, \text{eV}
\]  

Comparing:  
\[
5.79 \times 10^{-5} \, \text{eV} \ll 2.55 \, \text{eV}
\]  
Thus \(\langle H \rangle \ll \Delta E\).

Answer: B
MODEL_OUTPUT_END

