= \((\frac74\cos^2\alpha + \frac14\sin^2\alpha) + \frac{\sqrt3}{2}\sin\alpha\cos\alpha\).

Write \(\frac74\cos^2\alpha + \frac14\sin^2\alpha = \frac14(7\cos^2\alpha + \sin^2\alpha) = \frac14(6\cos^2\alpha + (\cos^2\alpha+\sin^2\alpha)) = \frac14(6\cos^2\alpha + 1)\).

So expression = \(\frac14(6\cos^2\alpha + 1) + \frac{\sqrt3}{2}\sin\alpha\cos\alpha\).

Set equal to \((19/14)^2 = 361/196\).

Multiply by 4: \(6\cos^2\alpha + 1 + 2\sqrt3\sin\alpha\cos\alpha = 361/49\).

So \(6\cos^2\alpha + 2\sqrt3\sin\alpha\cos\alpha = 361/49 - 1 = (361-49)/49 = 312/49\).

Divide by 2: \(3\cos^2\alpha + \sqrt3\sin\alpha\cos\alpha = 156/49\).

